A2 bounded-read iterator key-length preflight
Date: 2026-10-06

Change:
- Under a finite byte budget, ShardStore.visitResult probes the RocksDB iterator key into a reusable two-byte array to learn its complete logical length without allocating a complete Java key array.
- The key and value lengths are charged together before requesting full key/value arrays. A row that would exceed the remaining aggregate allowance is yielded without full Java key/value materialization.
- The real RocksDB regression uses a 2-byte key / 30-byte value followed by a 32-byte key / 1-byte value under a 50-byte budget. The first row is delivered; the second is denied. Actual bytes are 65, charged bytes are 32, visited rows are 1, and denied reads are 1.

