This only avoids full Java key/value array materialization for a row rejected by the remaining aggregate byte allowance. It does not bound RocksDB native work or RSS, iterator/index access, later visitor/projection allocations, legacy field limits, the full mutation envelope, production finite policy, or compatibility behavior. A2 remains `IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION`.
